{
  "id": "ECC.2",
  "number": "2",
  "bookId": "ECC",
  "reference": "Ecclesiastes 2",
  "verseCount": 26,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "2",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ECC 2"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "2",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I said in my heart, Come now, I will prove thee with mirth; therefore enjoy pleasure: and, behold, this also was vanity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I said of laughter, It is mad; and of mirth, What doeth it? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I searched in my heart how to cheer my flesh with wine, my heart yet guiding ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " with wisdom, and how to lay hold on folly, till I might see what it was good for the sons of men that they should do under heaven all the days of their life. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I made me great works; I builded me houses; I planted me vineyards; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I made me gardens and parks, and I planted trees in them of all kinds of fruit; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I made me pools of water, to water therefrom the forest where trees were reared; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I bought men-servants and maid-servants, and had servants born in my house; also I had great possessions of herds and flocks, above all that were before me in Jerusalem; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I gathered me also silver and gold, and the treasure of kings and of the provinces; I gat me men-singers and women-singers, and the delights of the sons of men, musical instruments, and that of all sorts. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So I was great, and increased more than all that were before me in Jerusalem: also my wisdom remained with me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And whatsoever mine eyes desired I kept not from them; I withheld not my heart from any joy; for my heart rejoiced because of all my labor; and this was my portion from all my labor. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I looked on all the works that my hands had wrought, and on the labor that I had labored to do; and, behold, all was vanity and a striving after wind, and there was no profit under the sun.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And I turned myself to behold wisdom, and madness, and folly: for what ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " the man ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " that cometh after the king? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " that which hath been done long ago. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I saw that wisdom excelleth folly, as far as light excelleth darkness. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The wise man’s eyes are in his head, and the fool walketh in darkness: and yet I perceived that one event happeneth to them all. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then said I in my heart, As it happeneth to the fool, so will it happen even to me; and why was I then more wise? Then said I in my heart, that this also is vanity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For of the wise man, even as of the fool, there is no remembrance for ever; seeing that in the days to come all will have been long forgotten. And how doth the wise man die even as the fool! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So I hated life, because the work that is wrought under the sun was grievous unto me; for all is vanity and a striving after wind.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And I hated all my labor wherein I labored under the sun, seeing that I must leave it unto the man that shall be after me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And who knoweth whether he will be a wise man or a fool? yet will he have rule over all my labor wherein I have labored, and wherein I have showed myself wise under the sun. This also is vanity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore I turned about to cause my heart to despair concerning all the labor wherein I had labored under the sun. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For there is a man whose labor is with wisdom, and with knowledge, and with skilfulness; yet to a man that hath not labored therein shall he leave it for his portion. This also is vanity and a great evil. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For what hath a man of all his labor, and of the striving of his heart, wherein he laboreth under the sun? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For all his days are ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " sorrows, and his travail is grief; yea, even in the night his heart taketh no rest. This also is vanity.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There is nothing better for a man ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " that he should eat and drink, and make his soul enjoy good in his labor. This also I saw, that it is from the hand of God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For who can eat, or who can have enjoyment, more than I? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 2:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For to the man that pleaseth him ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " giveth wisdom, and knowledge, and joy; but to the sinner he giveth travail, to gather and to heap up, that he may give to him that pleaseth God. This also is vanity and a striving after wind.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.2.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.2.26"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "ECC.3",
    "number": "3",
